# Comms public navigation

## Get started (toolkit chooser)

**Get started** in Header resolves to `/#toolkit` (Home: Comms / steward craft / run the local). Do **not** retarget Get started at `/brand-kit`. Brand Kit stays its own top-level link. The Comms path card on Home still sends empty kits to `/onboarding` and established kits to First week.

Brand Kit is the Comms home base (colours, logo, local number, links). First week (`/guide/social-media-plan`) is the channel roadmap after identity — listed under Guides → Comms.

## Header Guides menu (keep this shape)

Five groups in [`nav-config.ts`](src/components/layout/nav/nav-config.ts) `learnGroups` (trigger label **Guides**). Job groups (floor / local / campaign) live in [`guide-registry.ts`](src/lib/comms/guide-registry.ts). **Officer Learning Center** is a **top-level header link** (between Guides and Brand Kit) — not nested under Steward craft. Five columns at 2xl. Floor and The local start **collapsed** below 2xl (`<details>`), expanded at 2xl.

1. **Comms** — First week (`/guide/social-media-plan`), The Blueprint (`/guide`), Workshop outline (`/guide/workshop`)
2. **By channel** — Print Guide, Union Boards Guide, Website Guide, Email & outreach, Short-form video
3. **Steward craft** — Steward playbooks hub, Steward 101, Bargaining lifecycle, Strike operations (`/guide/strike`), Crisis comms
4. **Floor and the local** — nested **Floor** (grievance, DFR, RTR, seniority, joint committee, workplace mapping) and **The local** (union history, running meetings, bylaws, land acknowledgement, membership signup)
5. **Libraries** — Social Examples, Captions, Photo Consent, Brand Assets, Comms Resources

What's new, Built in solidarity, and Install stay in the **footer**, not the mega-menu.

Do not re-flatten channel guides into a long top-level link bar. Do not invent marketing routes (`/about`, `/pricing`, `/blog`) unless product expands. Do not add a sixth mega-menu column. New topic playbooks go in the Floor or The local subgroup (and `/guides` catalog) — not as extra top-level columns.

Footer row in the mega-menu: **All guides** → `/guides` catalog (Blueprint stays `/guide`). Do not point All guides at The Blueprint.

## Header Tools menu (keep this shape)

Five groups in `nav-config.ts` `toolGroups` (mega-menu columns). Group by **job** (what the steward is making), not by First week channel. Lesson: [`session-knowledge-2026-08-18-tools-catalog-ia.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-18-tools-catalog-ia.md) (four Comms jobs + Steward prep). Visual grid: 2-col → `xl` 3-col → `2xl` 5-col; panel is viewport-clamped (`flyout-geometry.ts`).

1. **Brand** — Logo Builder, Resizer, Document & Slide Generator
2. **Union boards** — Board Banner & Trim, Board Notice Maker, Solidarity Posters, QR Board Posters, Org Chart
3. **Print & cards** — Flyer Maker, QR Link Cards, Action Cards, Pulse Poll (Hub-signed-in only)
4. **Social & web** — Graphic Maker, Quote Card, Meeting Backgrounds, Website Template, Alt-Text Assistant
5. **Steward worksheets** — RTW & accommodation, Pre-disciplinary log, Complaint vs grievance, Bylaw Builder, Proposal Tracker, Rules of Order

Footer row in the mega-menu: **All tools** → `/tools` index. Do not re-flatten Tools into a single ungrouped list. Keep one **Tools ▾** trigger — do not add extra top-level tool links. Prefer extending an existing job group over inventing a sixth mega-menu column.

## Footer

Keep footer slim: product + legal. Include Tools (`/tools`), **Steward playbooks** (`/guide/steward-playbooks`), **Officer Learning** (`/guide/officer-learning` — same destination as the top-level header link), **Brand Kit**, **What's new**, **Built in solidarity**, Privacy, Security, Accessibility, Feedback.

Channel guides, Social Examples, Captions, Resources, Brand Assets, and Install as an app stay in Guides ▾ — do not re-inflate the footer with every Comms library link.

## Brand Assets

`/assets` lives under Guides → Libraries. Brand Kit may still link Brand Assets on-page.

## Auth chrome (session-aware)

When authenticated, the public header / mobile drawer always show **Officer Hub**, **Profile**, and **Sign out** (even if `NEXT_PUBLIC_OFFICER_HUB_PUBLIC` is false). When logged out, Officer Hub appears only if the hub is public. Profile photo capture lives at `/app/profile`.

## Keep out of public chrome

- Operator docs (`docs/guides/SETUP.md`, `DEPLOY.md`)
- Hub modules (use `HubNav`) — except the session-aware Officer Hub / Profile / Sign out controls above. Do **not** duplicate **Comms toolbox** inside `HubNav`; Tools / Guides / Brand Kit / the home mark already reach the public toolbox.
- Invented marketing routes (`/about`, `/pricing`, `/blog`) unless product expands. **What's new** (`/updates`) is the dated product-growth list, not a blog.

